<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">War of the Landshut Succession</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1503–1505</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The War of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/landshut">Landshut</a> Succession was fought in 1503–1505 over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria-landshut">Duchy of Bavaria-Landshut</a>. Duke George the Rich had left his lands to his son-in-law <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rupert-of-germany">Rupert of the Palatinate</a> in breach of Wittelsbach family agreements, and Albert IV of Bavaria-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a> went to war. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cologne">Cologne</a> arbitration of 1505 gave most of the lands to Albert, reuniting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palatinate-neuburg">Palatinate-Neuburg</a> was created for Rupert's sons.</p></div>
